<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly steady with only two-week to two-months showing dips, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a reflection of the excess money in the system,&quot; said a foreign bank dealer.</p>
<p>Traders, however, said banks did not adjust their swap rates as they had done so in the previous sessions after anticipating the liquidity in the system.</p>
<p>The nine-month economic growth figures due to be released this week could bring in more dollars from investors, they said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  NOV 27		NOV 26</p>
<p>    1 W		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		11  1/16		11  1/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/8		 11  1/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/16		11  1/4</p>
<p>    3 M		11  5/16		11  5/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  9/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  3/4		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    VAL		28-Nov		  27-Nov</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
